"If the finished character looks the same, why does the order matter? First, it is shared. Teachers, textbooks, and the ministry's website all teach the same order, so everyone can learn from everyone else. Second, the order follows the flow of the brush. The ministry explains that the second stroke of 日 ends with a small hook because the brush is already turning toward the next stroke inside the box.": "ec5c660871e8",
"In this lesson, choose a rule and watch the 3D brush write its example character, with numbers showing the order. Try writing it backward, too, and notice that the result can look similar even though the order is not the standard one. Then play Guess the Next Stroke, and practice the six example characters on the practice pad.": "c3da4d20367c",
